; ============================================================================
; AIF-087 M4 -- RECOVERY NON-REFIRE, STEP 2: POISON THE RECORD
;
; Status: CANDIDATE / explicit-run, driven from C++ by
;         run_trigger_recovery_nonrefire (REGRESSION TRIGGERVETO RECOVERY).
; Safety: MUTATING (SANDBOX only; the arm erases the fixture when it finishes)
;
; WHY THIS STEP EXISTS AT ALL. The committed write already put VETOED in the
; record, so replaying the journal would write the value that is ALREADY THERE
; and a green read would not distinguish "replay ran" from "replay did nothing".
; This overwrites the record with a THIRD value, so the later read has two
; possible answers and only one of them means the journal was replayed.
;
; THE WRITE IS DELIBERATELY UNBUFFERED -- a plain REPLACE under TABLE OFF, the
; direct-write path -- so it leaves NO journal of its own. A buffered write here
; would either need its own COMMIT (writing a second journal over the one the
; arm is about to restore) or would not land at all.
;
; SELF-CHECKING: if buffering were somehow still on from the SQLsel DML scope,
; the marker path reads the DBF rather than the buffer (measured: TRG_MR1 in
; trigger_veto_arm_multirep.dts asserts exactly that), so TRG_R0 would read .F.
; and the arm reds here rather than producing a meaningless recovery reading.
; ============================================================================

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX

FORMULA "TRGRECOV-POISON-BEGIN"

; The work script deliberately does not close. Close before opening: a USE over
; a table already open in the current area is a NO-OP, not an open (the WSENV
; finding, 2026-08-30), and a no-op here would leave the cursor on a table
; whose state this script has not established.
SELECT 1
CLOSE
USE TRGVETO
GO 1
REPLACE NAME WITH "STALE"
GO 1
? "TRG_R0_poison_landed:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "STALE")
CLOSE

FORMULA "TRGRECOV-POISON-END"
